# PATCH: 019-readonly-bookmarks
#
# Makes the bookmark store read-only: users cannot create, edit, move, reorder,
# or remove bookmarks. DenBrowser's curated shortcuts live on the custom new-tab
# page (patch 018) instead of the editable Firefox bookmark system.
#
# Enforcement is at the single service funnel — the public mutation methods of
# toolkit/components/places/Bookmarks.sys.mjs (insert, insertTree, update,
# moveToFolder, remove, eraseEverything, reorder). Each returns a rejected
# promise before doing any work, so every caller (star button, Library, context
# menus, keyboard shortcuts, drag-and-drop) fails uniformly. This is safe in
# this build because nothing seeds bookmarks programmatically: the Bookmarks
# enterprise policy is not used, Sync is disabled (patch 013), profile import is
# disabled, and NoDefaultBookmarks is set. The default bookmark roots are
# created by the Places database layer (C++), not these methods, so read paths
# (fetch/observers) are unaffected.
#
# NOTE: this is the hard block / enforcement layer. Hiding the now non-functional
# bookmark UI (star button, menus, context-menu items) is a separate cosmetic
# change, tuned against a real build.


diff --git a/toolkit/components/places/Bookmarks.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/places/Bookmarks.sys.mjs
